result.root_cause:
The curated templates were written as reference documents, not chat replies:
- the attribution sits in front of the answer ("Per the CvSU officials roster effective…");
- section labels are in ALL CAPS;
- every sub-topic of a broad intent is dumped in one block;
- the Filipino variants end with a formulaic "Salamat sa inyong tanong!".

_select_response then always serves the same English and Filipino variant (EN #0 / FIL #1), so the worst-styled long-form is exactly the one users see. Every serving copy (models/responses_map.json) and every retrain input (data/cavsu_intents.json, data/cavsu_intents.db) holds the same text, so the fix has to land in all three at once without a retrain.

result.summary:
Built the Tier 3 prompt de-leak and pushback workstream on top of the uncommitted work already in the tree. Nothing was reverted. Every test I ran passes: the 26 root test_*.py scripts (test_response_blocks.py skipped, as instructed) plus the new test_llm_reply_polish.py. The two polish test files (test_conversation_polish.py, now 24 cases, and test_llm_reply_polish.py) only exercise the code with stubs and a fake LLM. Nothing was run against a real local model or Claude.

**Prompt (api/hybrid_chatbot.py)**
- `build_scope_locked_prompt`: replaced the VOICE block (~line 341) with the shorter version from the design. It bans meta-phrases, says to answer the exact question first and offer a one-line follow-up, explains that short follow-ups like "why only trece?" refer to the previous answer, gives the pushback line ("I'm an offline assistant, so I can't browse live pages for you") and keeps the no-repeat / no-restated-assumption rule.
- The prompt with `build_scope_locked_prompt('P', None, None)` was 2792 characters before; it is now shorter, and a test fails if it grows past 2792.
- The refusal protocol, response rules, topic block and glossary are byte-identical.
- `_grounded_prompt` rule 6 now gives "batay sa mga excerpt" as its example in place of "the excerpts don't mention". Rules 1-5 and 7 and the static preamble are unchanged.

**Post-processor (api/conversation_polish.py)** — pure functions, no import of hybrid_chatbot.
- `strip_rag_meta` now also catches:
  - "official CvSU …" sources and coordinated nouns ("excerpts and conversation context");
  - "… I have" endings;
  - hedge prefixes ("I'm sorry, but …"), keeping the hedge;
  - lead-ins at the start of a later sentence on the same line;
  - bold-wrapped lead-ins;
  - "Based on the excerpts provided [X], …", rewritten to "According to [X], …" with the bracket moved byte-for-byte;
  - an orphaned "According to," left after the guard strips a citation;
  - "the excerpts mention only …" → "I only have details on …";
  - Filipino lead-ins (batay/base/ayon sa mga excerpt…). "impormasyon"/"datos" only match with ibinigay/binigay, so "Ayon sa Registrar, …" is left alone;
  - Filipino "Hindi nabanggit sa mga excerpt ang …" and the inline "sa mga excerpt".
- It never touches "[OUT_OF_SCOPE]" or text inside brackets, and running it twice gives the same result.
- New functions:
  - `dedupe_reply(reply, previous) -> (reply, repeated)`: drops paragraphs and list items repeated inside one reply. Across turns it only flags a repeat (similarity ratio ≥ 0.85, or ≥ 80% of non-trivial lines already in the previous reply) and never trims.
  - `is_pushback`, `is_live_lookup`, `wants_repeat`.
  - `pivot_reply(filipino, live_lookup)`: canned EN/FIL text with no CvSU facts; the only URL is https://cvsu.edu.ph.

**Wiring in `predict()` Step 3 (hybrid_chatbot.py ~2714-2790)**
- New helper `_last_bot_response` (~line 1912).
- After both gates pass and before `_gather_grounding`: if there is a previous turn and the message is both a pushback and a live-lookup ask ("just create a list available online"), it returns the pivot labelled "<Claude LLM|Local LLM> (pushback)" and never calls the LLM.
- After a passing output guard:
  - `strip_rag_meta` runs again, to clean orphans left by the citation strip;
  - then `dedupe_reply` runs. A cross-turn repeat returns a pivot labelled "… (repeat-pivot)", unless the user asked for a repeat or re-asked the identical question. This sits before the prose-refusal check.
- Labels never contain "(out-of-scope)" and start with "Claude LLM" or "Local LLM", so `_classify_source` still maps them to LLM_*.
- If the reply is empty after scrubbing, the turn falls through to the existing degraded path (verbatim tier / llm_unavailable) instead of returning an empty string.
- Untouched: the refusal-token path, the guard's reject paths, `LLM_GUARD_MESSAGE`, the verbatim tier, Step 0.9.

**Tests**
- test_conversation_polish.py: new strip cases (including negatives and idempotence), plus DedupeTests and PushbackTests.
- test_llm_reply_polish.py: a stub bot runs through `predict()` covering:
  - lead-in stripped with the citation kept;
  - the refusal token still wins;
  - an invented citation stripped with no orphan left;
  - an invented email still withheld;
  - a block repeated inside one reply dropped;
  - repeat pivot vs. "can you repeat that" vs. the same question re-asked;
  - the pushback shortcut skips the LLM;
  - pushback with no previous turn, and "what is on the website for admission", still reach the LLM;
  - prompt contents and length.

**Line endings:** api/hybrid_chatbot.py is CRLF. One `sed -i` call converted it to LF, so I immediately converted all 3308 lines back to CRLF. `git diff --stat` shows only the expected hunks.
